            <ArticleTitle>A giant circumflex coronary artery aneurysm with a fistula into the coronary sinus: case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E151-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1532/hsf.1368</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery fistulas are a rare clinical entity in cardiac anomalies, and in a significant portion of patients, the fistulas are accompanied by coronary aneurysm formation. In this article, we present a giant circumflex coronary artery aneurysm with a fistula into the coronary sinus.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
